#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:2
msgid "Assertions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:4
msgid ""
"An assertion is a digitally signed document that either verifies the "
"validity of a process, as attested by the signer, or carries policy "
"information, as formulated by the signer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:6
msgid ""
"[Snapcraft](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/), {ref}`snapd "
"<ref-glossary_snapd>`, the [Snap Store](https://snapcraft.io/store) and "
"[Brand stores](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/brand-stores) all use assertions "
"to handle a variety of functions and processes, including authentication, "
"policy setting, identification and validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:8
msgid ""
"Assertions are text-based and take a context-dependent format that always "
"includes one or more headers, an optional body, and the encoded signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:10
msgid "Assertion types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:12
msgid "These are the currently used assertion types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:14
msgid ""
"**[account](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/account)**: "
"links an account name to its identifier and other properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:15
msgid ""
"**[account-key](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/account-"
"key)**: holds the public part of a key belonging to the account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:16
msgid ""
"**[model](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/model)**: brand-"
"specified properties for the device, used to drive the building of an Ubuntu "
"Core image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:17
msgid ""
"**[serial](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/serial)**: "
"binds the device identity to the device's key by carrying the public part"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:18
msgid ""
"**[snap-build](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/snap-"
"build)**: the basic properties of a snap at the time it was built by the "
"developer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:19
msgid ""
"**[snap-declaration](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/snap-"
"declaration)**:  defines various snap properties, such as `snap-id`, its "
"name, and the publisher, plus policy related to accessing privileged "
"interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:20
msgid ""
"**[snap-revision](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/snap-"
"revision)**: store acknowledgement on receipt of a snap build labelled with "
"a revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:21
msgid ""
"**[store](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/store)**: "
"defines the configuration needed to connect a device to a store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:22
msgid ""
"**[system-user](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/system-"
"user)**: usually brand authorisation to create local system users on "
"specified devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:23
msgid ""
"**[validation](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/"
"validation)**: validates a specific snap revision for a given series"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:24
msgid ""
"**[validation-set](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/"
"validation-set)**: a group of snaps that are either installed or permitted "
"to be installed together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:26
msgid "Assertion format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:28
msgid "The typical format of an assertion, with common headers, is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:30
msgid ""
"type:          <type>       # For example, “account” or “model”\n"
"authority-id:  <account id> # On whose authority this assertion is made\n"
"<key field 1>: <value>      # Fields identifying the object of the "
"assertion\n"
"...\n"
"<key field N>: <value>\n"
"<other field>: <value>\n"
"...\n"
"revision: <int>             # Assertions can be updated with a higher "
"revision\n"
"format: <int>               # Assertion types can have backward incompatible "
"format changes signaled by a higher format\n"
"body-length: <int>          # Present if a body is provided with this "
"assertion\n"
"sign-key-sha3-384: <key id> # Encoded key id of signing key\n"
"\n"
"<body>                      # Optional type-dependent body of length `body-"
"length` bytes\n"
"\n"
"<signature>                 # Encoded signature\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:48
msgid "every assertion has `type`, `sign-key-sha3-384` and a signature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:49
msgid "most assertions have `authority-id`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:50
msgid "values are scalars (strings, integers, booleans), lists, or maps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:51
msgid ""
"some headers are used as a unique index to specify the context of an "
"assertion of the given, together they form the so-called primary key of the "
"assertion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:52
msgid ""
"most assertions also have a revision to enable a particular assertion to be "
"updated by issuing another assertion of the same type and index with a "
"higher revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:54
msgid ""
"Given a particular type and index, there is only one “latest” valid "
"assertion that properly determines policy for a system - the one with the "
"highest revision. For a given assertion, the index headers must all be "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:56
msgid "Viewing assertions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:58
msgid ""
"The `snap known <type> [<header>=<value>...]` command can be used to view "
"assertions or a specific type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:60
msgid ""
"$ snap known account account-id=generic\n"
"type: account\n"
"authority-id: canonical\n"
"account-id: generic\n"
"display-name: Generic\n"
"timestamp: 2017-07-27T00:00:00.0Z\n"
"username: generic\n"
"validation: certified\n"
"sign-key-sha3-384: [...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:72
msgid ""
"Similarly, a snap's assertions are downloaded alongside the snap using the "
"`snap download` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:74
msgid ""
"$ snap download gnome-calculator\n"
"Fetching snap \"gnome-calculator\"\n"
"Fetching assertions for \"gnome-calculator\"\n"
"Install the snap with:\n"
"   snap ack gnome-calculator_945.assert\n"
"   snap install gnome-calculator_945.snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:83
msgid "Encoded sha3-384 differences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:85
msgid ""
"Assertions include a `snap-sha3-384` hash value to ensure their integrity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:87
msgid "snap-sha3-384: j73cFx0pIMoX4U[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:91
msgid ""
"However, these hash values will appear different, depending on whether they "
"were either downloaded from the Snap Store, such as with the `snap download` "
"command, or retrieved with via the  snapd REST API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:93
msgid ""
"This difference is because the Store uses hex-encoded byte arrays while the "
"snapd REST API encodes hashes with with _base64_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/assertions.md:95
msgid ""
"Developers can typically use hash-encoded values directly in their code, "
"whereas _base64_ values will need to be decoded first, such as with the "
"[base64](https://manpages.ubuntu.com/manpages/jammy/en/man1/base64.1.html) "
"command."
msgstr ""
